            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0080" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg76"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.116/169: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-27T15:00:00+08:00">October 27, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>631 [<hi rendition="#italic">641</hi>]. Tientsin’s 195, October 18, 4 p.m. The
                    Embassy on October 25th made representations to the Japanese Embassy on the <pb
                        facs="0081" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/> basis of Tientsin’s aforementioned
                    telegram and previous communications. The concerned Japanese official yesterday
                    informed the Embassy that discussions were now proceeding with the Tientsin
                    Customs regarding the matter and that the Embassy would be kept informed of
                    developments.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tientsin, Chungking and Shanghai. By mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
